From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:27:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] output: A shown OSK stays on top of a fullscreen view

Over a fullscreen view the top layer, and with it the OSK, was only
drawn while that view had an input method enabled. Apps that never
enable one, like games through SDL or DOSBox, get the OSK unfolded by
hand or over D-Bus: it was mapped, yet stayed behind the view and only
came up while the screen was touched.

Reveal the shell while the OSK is mapped. Stevia unmaps its surface
when folded, so nothing shows over a fullscreen video otherwise.
---
 src/output.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/output.c b/src/output.c
index 9ffac0a..abcc3eb 100644
--- a/src/output.c
+++ b/src/output.c
@@ -2600,6 +2600,15 @@ should_reveal_shell (PhocOutput *self)
     }
   }
 
+  /* Is the OSK shown over our fullscreen view? Apps that never enable an input method (games
+   * through SDL, DOSBox) get it unfolded by hand or over D-Bus; it stayed hidden behind them and
+   * only came up while the screen was touched. Stevia unmaps its surface when folded. */
+  if (phoc_view_is_mapped (self->fullscreen_view)) {
+    PhocLayerSurface *osk = phoc_layer_shell_find_osk (self);
+    if (osk && phoc_layer_surface_get_mapped (osk))
+      return true;
+  }
+
   /* Is some draggable surface unfolded, being dragged or animated? */
   wl_list_for_each (layer_surface, &self->layer_surfaces, link) {
     PhocDraggableLayerSurface *draggable;
